---
title: Whole roast chicken
servings: 4
tags: [american, chicken, weeknight]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour 35 minutes
source: Weeknight Roast Chicken by America's Test Kitchen, https://wskg.org/americas-test-kitchen-weeknight-roast-chicken
---

Put a 12-inch #oven-safe skillet{} on the middle rack and heat the oven to
450°F with the pan inside.

Mix the @kosher salt{1%tbsp} with the @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Pat the @whole chicken{1}(3 1/2 to 4 lb, giblets removed) dry. Rub it all over
with the @olive oil{1%tbsp}, then season it evenly with the salt mix. Tie the
legs together with #kitchen twine{} and tuck the wing tips under the back.

Set the chicken breast side up in the hot skillet. Roast ~{30%minutes}, until
the breast reads 120°F and the thighs 135°F.

Turn the oven off and leave the chicken in, door shut, ~{30%minutes} more,
until the breast reads 160°F and the thighs 175°F.

Move it to a board and rest, uncovered, ~{20%minutes} before carving.

> Check both readings with a #thermometer{}: the times run 25 to 35 minutes
> each, depending on the bird.
